                <pb facs="1057" n="921" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg921"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 126.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Whitney to Mr.
                            Bayard.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Navy Department</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1888-09-19"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 19,
                        1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith, for
                    the information of the Department of State, a copy of a dispatch, dated the 10th
                    instant, from Commander C. M. Chester, commanding the U. S. S. <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Galena</hi>, reporting the result of his recent visit to
                    Port au Prince.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">W. C.
                        Whitney.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
